From: Nouveau diagnostic follow-up
Subject: [DIAGNOSTIC] nouveau: separate BAR2 map and access log budgets

The BAR2 map diagnostic currently uses one ratelimit state for mapping
lifecycle records and fast access records. A short burst of accesses can use
the entire budget before a relevant mapping is logged. Give the two record
classes independent, still bounded budgets so access traffic cannot hide map
creation/eviction/destruction events.

This is diagnostic-only. It does not change BAR2 mappings or access behavior.
Each record class remains limited to eight records per second.

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nvkm/subdev/instmem/nv50.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nvkm/subdev/instmem/nv50.c
@@ -42,0 +43 @@
+static DEFINE_RATELIMIT_STATE(nv50_instobj_diag_map_rs, HZ, 8);
@@ -92 +93 @@
-	if (!pages || !__ratelimit(&nv50_instobj_diag_access_rs))
+	if (!pages || !__ratelimit(&nv50_instobj_diag_map_rs))
@@ -96 +97 @@
-		 "NOUVEAU_DIAG_BAR2_MAP stage=%s pages=0x%x object=%p "
+		 "NOUVEAU_DIAG_BAR2_MAP budget=lifecycle stage=%s pages=0x%x object=%p "
